hadiths[4]{hadithnumber,text}:
"28176","Husayn and Abu Nuaym said: Israil narrated to us, on the authority of Zayd ibn Jubayr, on the authority of Abu Yazid al-Danni, on the authority of Maymunah bint Sad, freedwoman of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked about the child of adultery. He said: There is no good in him, two sandals with which I strive in the path of Allah are more beloved to me than to free a child of adultery."
"28177","Abu Nuaym narrated to us, Israil narrated to us, on the authority of Zayd ibn Jubayr, on the authority of Abu Yazid al-Danni, on the authority of Maymunah, freedwoman of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked about a man who kissed his wife while fasting. He said: He has broken fast."
"28178","Ali ibn Bahr narrated to us, he said: Isa narrated to us, he said: Thawr narrated to us, on the authority of Ziyad ibn Abi Sawdah, on the authority of his brother, that Maymunah, freedwoman of the Prophet, said: O Prophet of Allah, give us a ruling about Bayt al-Maqdis. He said: The land of resurrection and gathering, go to it and pray in it, for a prayer in it is like a thousand prayers in other than it. She said: What of one who cannot bear to travel to it or come to it? He said: Let him gift to it oil to be lit in it, for whoever gifts to it is as one who prayed in it."
"28179","Abu Musa al-Harawi narrated to us, he said: Isa ibn Yunus narrated to us with his chain, and he mentioned the like of it."
